{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The idol.</b> It is what is hewn from stone or wood:" "<b>Poured.</b> Like 'a molten calf' (Exodus 32:4):" "<b>He overlays it.</b> Like 'and they hammered out the gold plates' (Exodus 39:3), and from the root of רקיע (Genesis 1:7):" "<b>And fasten it.</b> Like 'make the chain' (Ezekiel 7:23) — in the form of chains:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:10.506999991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}